1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,491
Everyone in this party reads the same room.

2
00:00:03,391 --> 00:00:05,974
But one of them came aboard with a question of her own,

3
00:00:06,424 --> 00:00:09,438
and it's listed on her handheld, under her name.

4
00:00:11,238 --> 00:00:12,785
Whose suits are these?

5
00:00:13,685 --> 00:00:17,213
Today you give one person a quest that's theirs,

6
00:00:17,663 --> 00:00:19,471
and you make it lead somewhere.

7
00:00:20,671 --> 00:00:23,548
This is the doctor's handheld, aboard the hulk,

8
00:00:23,998 --> 00:00:25,919
with its Tasks app open.

9
00:00:26,819 --> 00:00:29,322
The row under her name is a side story,

10
00:00:29,772 --> 00:00:32,836
and the rows under Party are the ship's quests.

11
00:00:34,636 --> 00:00:36,743
A side story is a quest.

12
00:00:37,643 --> 00:00:39,953
It has the fields you learned in Class 1,

13
00:00:40,403 --> 00:00:43,344
and it lives in a section of its own, at the end of the file.

14
00:00:45,144 --> 00:00:46,922
What's new is this line.

15
00:00:47,372 --> 00:00:49,167
For, and then a job.

16
00:00:50,067 --> 00:00:53,359
A quest in your Quests section belongs to the whole ship.

17
00:00:53,809 --> 00:00:55,514
This one belongs to one person.

18
00:00:57,314 --> 00:00:58,362
It starts at once,

19
00:00:58,812 --> 00:00:59,962
it has an objective,

20
00:01:00,412 --> 00:01:05,082
and it's done when a signal arrives. Lint warns twice,

21
00:01:05,532 --> 00:01:07,066
and both warnings are true for now.

22
00:01:07,516 --> 00:01:09,113
Nothing sends that signal yet,

23
00:01:09,563 --> 00:01:11,299
and nothing hands the story out.

24
00:01:12,199 --> 00:01:15,242
The word after For is a job from your roster,

25
00:01:15,692 --> 00:01:18,832
or it can be a person: their key, or their name.

26
00:01:20,032 --> 00:01:21,743
So first, the signal.

27
00:01:22,643 --> 00:01:25,150
On the doctor's handheld, in the airlock,

28
00:01:25,600 --> 00:01:28,280
her reading is the button that should finish her story.

29
00:01:30,080 --> 00:01:34,141
In the file I find that choice, the one only the surgeon is offered,

30
00:01:34,591 --> 00:01:37,183
and I add a second outcome after the first,

31
00:01:37,633 --> 00:01:41,734
with a comma between them. Learn the fact, comma, send the signal.

32
00:01:42,634 --> 00:01:45,627
The name has to match the story's, letter for letter.

33
00:01:46,527 --> 00:01:48,585
And don't lose that comma.

34
00:01:49,035 --> 00:01:51,309
Without it, the signal is never sent.

35
00:01:52,509 --> 00:01:53,469
Then the handing out.

36
00:01:54,369 --> 00:01:55,601
I open the story file

37
00:01:56,051 --> 00:01:58,213
and find the card from Lecture 2.

38
00:01:59,113 --> 00:02:01,611
One line on it starts the visit,

39
00:02:02,061 --> 00:02:06,650
and I add a few words to the end of that line. Stories equals,

40
00:02:07,100 --> 00:02:10,027
and then the section of the fact sheet to read them from.

41
00:02:10,927 --> 00:02:14,080
The key in quotes is the key on my Side Stories heading.

42
00:02:15,880 --> 00:02:17,272
That's the whole change.

43
00:02:18,172 --> 00:02:21,935
From now on each person is handed their story as they beam down,

44
00:02:22,385 --> 00:02:25,464
and that includes someone who beams down late.

45
00:02:26,664 --> 00:02:28,268
The engineer gets one too.

46
00:02:29,168 --> 00:02:32,283
Here it is on his handheld, under his name,

47
00:02:32,733 --> 00:02:34,984
and it's finished by his own reading.

48
00:02:36,784 --> 00:02:38,465
And a side story can lead on,

49
00:02:38,915 --> 00:02:42,004
the same way any quest does, with Then.

50
00:02:42,904 --> 00:02:46,479
When the surgeon's story completes, it sends a second signal,

51
00:02:46,929 --> 00:02:50,562
and a quest for the whole ship is waiting to hear it.

52
00:02:52,362 --> 00:02:54,008
So read the chain from the top.

53
00:02:54,458 --> 00:02:56,241
She reads the tags.

54
00:02:56,691 --> 00:02:58,614
That finishes her story.

55
00:02:59,064 --> 00:03:01,218
Her story finishes the ship's quest,

56
00:03:01,668 --> 00:03:02,805
and the ship is paid.

57
00:03:03,705 --> 00:03:06,680
A story can carry a reward of its own as well,

58
00:03:07,130 --> 00:03:09,804
and it's paid to the ship that person came from.

59
00:03:11,604 --> 00:03:13,845
The ship's quest gets a page,

60
00:03:14,295 --> 00:03:16,815
because the Quest Log shows all of it.

61
00:03:17,715 --> 00:03:20,367
This is the Quest Log on Helm's handheld.

62
00:03:20,817 --> 00:03:24,809
A heading, and two bullets with a small picture for a dot.

63
00:03:25,709 --> 00:03:29,326
In the file, the word after icon names the picture.

64
00:03:31,126 --> 00:03:33,461
The side story stays short.

65
00:03:33,911 --> 00:03:36,074
Tasks only shows its heading.

66
00:03:37,274 --> 00:03:41,962
Four rules. A side story is a bonus, and never the only way,

67
00:03:42,412 --> 00:03:45,252
because nobody covers for a person.

68
00:03:46,152 --> 00:03:48,724
One job word goes in three places:

69
00:03:49,174 --> 00:03:52,409
the roster, the story, and the choice that finishes it.

70
00:03:53,309 --> 00:03:56,197
For takes one job, or one person.

71
00:03:57,097 --> 00:03:58,717
And one story goes to one person.

72
00:04:00,517 --> 00:04:01,561
Lint is good here.

73
00:04:02,011 --> 00:04:04,258
It tells you when a story is for nobody,

74
00:04:04,708 --> 00:04:07,948
and it tells you when two outcomes have run together.

75
00:04:09,148 --> 00:04:13,439
I play it twice, and each time Helm stays on the bridge to watch.

76
00:04:14,339 --> 00:04:16,048
First the doctor goes across.

77
00:04:16,498 --> 00:04:18,518
On her handheld I go back one step,

78
00:04:18,968 --> 00:04:21,235
and the list there has three rows now,

79
00:04:21,685 --> 00:04:23,831
and the third one is Tasks.

80
00:04:24,731 --> 00:04:26,823
There's her story, under her name.

81
00:04:28,623 --> 00:04:30,465
She reads the tags,

82
00:04:30,915 --> 00:04:32,430
and the bridge is told twice:

83
00:04:32,880 --> 00:04:36,517
her story is complete, and so is the ship's quest.

84
00:04:38,317 --> 00:04:40,320
Then the chief goes across alone,

85
00:04:40,770 --> 00:04:42,147
and that's a short crew.

86
00:04:43,047 --> 00:04:46,860
He's offered her reading as the last button, marked as covering,

87
00:04:47,310 --> 00:04:49,123
and the party learns the fact.

88
00:04:50,023 --> 00:04:52,359
But her story was never handed out,

89
00:04:52,809 --> 00:04:55,463
so the ship's quest stays open.

90
00:04:57,263 --> 00:05:00,625
Then he reads his own record, and his story completes.

91
00:05:01,525 --> 00:05:06,122
The next lecture shows you the way round that open quest.

92
00:05:07,322 --> 00:05:09,393
Write a story for your third person,

93
00:05:09,843 --> 00:05:11,345
finished by their own reading.

94
00:05:12,245 --> 00:05:16,232
Give the chief's story somewhere to lead. Then break it.

95
00:05:16,682 --> 00:05:18,848
Misspell the job after For,

96
00:05:19,298 --> 00:05:20,585
read what lint says,

97
00:05:21,035 --> 00:05:22,478
and play it once anyway.

98
00:05:24,278 --> 00:05:25,830
Next time is the checkpoint:

99
00:05:26,280 --> 00:05:29,753
one away scene of your own, planned on paper and played.
